# Cursor engineering (Texoma Dashboard)

Treat the agent as a senior engineer, not autocomplete.

## Scope

- One feature / one layer / one PR-sized change at a time
- Prefer: types → client/mapper → Route Handler → UI → tests (do not generate everything at once)
- Prefer explain architecture and wait when the user asks for design first

## Reuse before create

- Search the repo for an existing component, hook, service, schema, or util before adding a new one
- Do not duplicate API client patterns — extend `src/lib/nexhealth` and `src/lib/ghl`

## Structure

- One responsibility per file (UI vs validation vs API vs mappers)
- Prefer colocated feature folders when adding new domains; otherwise match `src/app` / `src/components` / `src/lib`
- Keep React components ideally under ~200 lines (max ~250); split when larger

## Quality defaults

- Strong typing (no `any` unless unavoidable); no magic numbers — named constants
- DRY: extract shared utils when duplicates appear; behavior unchanged
- Comments only where intent is non-obvious

## After each feature

Review for: bugs, security, performance, accessibility, maintainability — then refactor if needed before commit.
